<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids mostly lower.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids mostly lower.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring wheat bids were mostly lower on Thursday as farmers began to move their wheat, several dealers said.</p>
<p>Soft white wheat bids were also weaker but movement was slow, several Pacific Northwest merchandisers said.</p>
<p>Warmer weather in the Dakotas, Montana and Minnesota prompted the selling. &quot;Trains are moving again,&quot; a Montana dealer said. &quot;There was a little movement today and there was better weather in North Dakota,&quot; another dealer said.</p>
<p>MGE spring wheat futures closed lower with March down 3-1/2 cents at $3.83-1/4 a bushel.  </p>
